  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "While Fang Yuan uses refinement formation rain on Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable’s underwater formation in regret crying sea, progress slows, then hits a brick. This is an earth path rank seven Immortal Gu. Its body is flat like a disk, yellowish brown, with a head and a tail, and four tentacles that look like hooks, growing evenly around the disk. Fang Yuan recognizes territory Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          1904
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "char_paradise_earth_immortal_venerable",
          "sys_immortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Territory Gu is very commonly seen, especially in Southern Border. Many villages, even if they are not proficient in earth path, try to get a rank three or four territory Gu. The village plants this Gu in the soil and lets a Gu Master in a position of authority use it, to raise and maintain control over this territory. It is a very useful Gu worm but very expensive, often used by forces. Individual Gu Masters did not need it. Territory Immortal Gu was kept within Dragon Whale Paradise. Fang Yuan can conveniently use this Gu worm to manage his immortal aperture and alter the landscape of the territory that he creates using territory Gu. Even if it were not useful, he still has to refine this earth path Immortal Gu. It is the key obstacle stopping him from progressing further.",
        "chapters": [
          1904
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "reg_southern_border",
          "sys_gu_master",
          "sys_gu_worms",
          "fac_gu_masters",
          "loc_dragon_whale_paradise"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The obstacle of territory Gu blocks Fang Yuan and the other Gu Immortals. No matter how they activate the supplementary formation, they cannot penetrate the formation anymore. After Fang Yuan modifies the supplementary formations and gives instructions for how to activate them, he uses refinement formation rain and refines territory Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          1905
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "formation-obstacle",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_immortal"
        ]
      }
    ]
